cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these certificates or verifiers, please cite this release."
title: "MathIS Sidon Frontier: Exact Symmetric and Two-Sided Certificates"
authors:
  - family-names: "Williams"
    given-names: "Ariel M."
version: "1.5.0"
date-released: "2026-10-23"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/FromAriel/mathis-sidon-frontier"
abstract: >-
  Exact symmetric and asymmetric two-sided Sidon smoothing certificates,
  standalone standard-library Python verifiers and reproducible preservation.
  Version 1.5.0 adds a compact exact centered-box witness with 2048 kernels at
  M=4096 and L=30, proving sqrt(ab) < 11785113371/12500000000 =
  0.942809069680 in the original Hou-Zhao finite symmetric model. Exact replay
  reconstructs all 122881 covers and energy values without a numerical solver.
  A fixed-family proof and prospective finite error bound accompany the witness.
  Earlier R9, R16, two-sided and v1.4.0 symmetric packages retain their bytes
  and historical scope. Hou-Zhao, Akwei, Chen, Wu/wustep and classical
  renewal/filter methods receive explicit attribution. No current record,
  significant new generic theorem, global optimality, exponent advance or
  solution of Erdos Problem 30 is claimed. Development, drafting and review
  used AI-assisted workflows. The new version DOI is pending; the reference
  below identifies the existing release series.
keywords:
  - Sidon sets
  - additive combinatorics
  - exact rational certificate
  - computer-assisted proof
  - Mathematical Integrity System
license: MIT
